.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log

# Built on demand by `echo-memory skill --package`. The source of truth is the
# SKILL.md that ships inside the package; a zip in git is a binary nobody can
# diff and goes stale the first time the instructions change.
echo-memory-skill.zip

# Runtime state written by agent tooling that runs inside this repo
# (claude-flow / ruflo). Local scratch: session state, a vector store and two
# SQLite databases, about 3MB of binaries that no one can diff and that say
# nothing about the project.
#
# Ignored rather than left untracked because `git add -A` is a normal thing to
# type. These appeared mid-session on 2026-09-09 and would have been swept into
# the next commit; they were checked for credentials and client data first and
# were clean, which is luck rather than a property of the arrangement.
#
# .claude/ is deliberately NOT here: skills and settings in it are worth
# sharing, and the day that changes it should be an explicit decision.
.claude-flow/
.swarm/
ruvector.db

# Same tool, same failure, found later: ruflo writes its adopted policy and the
# hash of it into .claude/ rather than .claude-flow/, so the rule above did not
# cover them and `git add -A` swept both into an unrelated commit on 2026-09-29.
# They are a benchmark result and a content hash for one machine's local tuning,
# which is not something another checkout should inherit.
.claude/proven-config.json
.claude/.proven-config-version

# Worktrees created for background agents. Each is its own checkout of this
# repository; committing one nests a git repo inside a git repo.
.claude/worktrees/
